  "source": {
    "title": "Lurgan Mail, 21 January 1905, p. 8 (\"Portadown Municipal Election\"); Belfast News-Letter, 18 January 1905, p. 3 (\"Portadown\")",
    "publisher": "Lurgan Mail (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "every figure read from both page images; they agree"
  },
  "note": "Triennial election of the whole council (fifteen seats, one area), polled in the Town Hall on Monday 16 January 1905 (15 January was a Sunday). Twenty-one candidates: eleven retiring members and ten new. After a dispute over a council appointment the Orange Club nominated its own candidates, W. J. Johnston and R. Courtney (retiring members), Robert Anderson, Valentine Wilson and W. H. Wright, and recommended the retiring members C. Johnston, C. Courtney and J. Davison; all eight were elected. The Lurgan Mail called it the first time in the municipal history of the town that the Orange body had put a direct issue to the electorate. Retiring members defeated: J. C. Fulton, J.P., and John Acheson, J.P. The electorate, poll and spoiled papers are not given. No party labels printed."
}
